WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.731
A correlated scalar and a pre-aggregated join can
sometimes produce the same result The

00:00:06.758 --> 00:00:12.402
correlated form may be simpler to read The
derived-table form may be

00:00:12.428 --> 00:00:18.030
convenient when several aggregated features are
needed Do not assume one

00:00:18.056 --> 00:00:23.873
form is always faster PostgreSQL can transform
queries during

00:00:23.899 --> 00:00:29.500
optimization Use correct semantics first then
inspect the plan

00:00:29.526 --> 00:00:30.895
on representative data
